 "conclusion": "On 15,202 assessments over 15,103 cells, 968 prompts and 1011 people, the compiled rule changes individual service by a median of -0.0667 and a mean of -0.07193, with the 1st-to-99th percentile running -0.2702 to +0.0994. ABSOLUTE HARM at the pre-registered eps=0.01: 12.46% of people are worse off, bootstrap [10.39%,14.54%], against a paired-shuffle floor of 10.63% whose 97.5th percentile is 12.07%: excess +1.83%, permutation p = 0.0100. The replicated cells give an independent, permutation-free floor: 95 cells, 99 df, per-person resolution 0.0742 at the median workload, and deconvolving that noise leaves a true harmed fraction of 8.18%. The worst-served 10% carry mean loss 0.5533 under full and 0.5059 under core (-0.0474). Gains are concentrated at Gini 0.463, the top decile taking 27% of all improvement. The positive control plants harm on 10% of raters and needs g=0.1 before it recovers half the plant -- an increment of +5.84% on a 10% plant -- so the harm rate resolves only shifts of that size and larger. ",
